hey everyone and welcome to my tutorial  on how to make a paper rocket ship  making the rocket ship will be the  trickiest origami model that I have  taught you how to make so far but I will  go through each step and every fold in  detail and try to simplify things as  best I can  there are a lot of similar folds  involved in making the paper balloon and  also the origami crane that you will  also see when making the paper rocket  ship so if you don't know how to already  make the balloon and the crane I highly  recommend that you watch my tutorials on  how to do those first before trying to  make the rocket ship making the rocket  ship requires that we have a square  piece of paper so if you're using a  piece of printer paper what you do is  you take this corner and you fold it  until this edge is lined up make a  crease and then you're going to cut off  the excess paper so now you should have  a piece of square paper that has a  diagonal fold in it now that we have a  square piece of paper with the diagonal  fold going this way we're going to take  this corner and fold the paper in half  until it meets this corner and then we  make a crease then you open up the paper  again and we're going to fold it in half  going this way this time and then you  make another crease now if you open up  the paper you should see an X and also a  horizontal fold as well fold the paper  in half on that horizontal fold then  what we do is we lift up this first  sheet and we're going to tuck this  corner in all the way down in the middle  just like that so lift it up and you  tuck this corner in like that and then  you make a crease do the same for the  left side  so you should have something that looks  just like this then what we're going to  do is we're going to fold each of these  flaps all the way up until the tip of  the flap meets the top of this triangle  do the same for the remaining three  flaps flip it over now you should have  something that looks just like this you  might recognize this from when we made  the paper balloon now what we're going  to do is something called a squash fold  what we do is we take these flaps and we  open up the middle of it which is sort  of like a pocket and if you open it up  you'll see that this corner wants to go  down and what you do is you push it down  until this corner meets the bottom of  this diamond so you take the flap open  it up all the way and then you push down  until this corner meets here and then  what you do is you make two creases one  here and one here so now you should have  something that looks just like this and  you want to do that for the remaining  three flaps  now we're going to do something that's  known as the pedal fold which you may  remember from my crane tutorial when we  were making the wings of the bird what  we need to do is we need to take each of  these corners here and we're going to  fold it so that this edge is on this  line that you see here this diagonal  line so we take it and we fold it until  it's on that line  so you should have something that looks  like that and you want to do that for  both sides so we have three more to go  now what we have to do is we have to  unfold these corners which we just fold  it in all right so these folds and  creases which we just made were to make  the petal fold a little bit easier what  you want to do now is you want to lift  up this corner here and you want to kind  of push it up and pull it until these  corners start to tuck in towards the  center so you lift it up and you'll see  that these corner pieces will start to  tuck in towards the center and what you  want to do is you want to just flatten  it out so you just tuck them in and then  you're just going to flatten the whole  thing out and you want to do that for  the remaining three so let's go ahead  and do that  now what we're going to do is we're just  going to fold these petal structures in  half so fold it down and do that for the  remaining three all right so this next  fold that I'm going to show you is not  tricky but you want to watch carefully  as I do it to make sure you're doing it  correctly if these petals are kind of  sticking out what you do is just put  your thumb at the bottom here to hold  them down then you're going to open  these two flaps on the right and what we  want to do is we want to take this  vertical edge this edge right here and  we're going to fold it backwards until  it meets this middle line here that  separates these two flaps so we want to  take this and we're going to fold it  backwards just like that until it gets  right into the center and then we're  going to just squish it down and flatten  it so you should have something that  looks just like this and then you want  to do that for the remaining three flaps  so now you should have something that  looks just like this now what we're  going to do is we're going to take the  tips of these petals and we're kind of  just going to let them swing outwards so  we're just going to swing it open and as  you'll see a little hood is formed what  you want to do with that hood is you  just want to squash it so just push  right down on it just like that then  we're going to do it for the remaining  three so open this let it swing open and  then you just push down on that hood  flip it over and do the same thing okay  so now what you want to do is you want  to take this little corner on the bottom  here and you want to tuck it up inside  of the rocket as far up as it will go  just like that and then you want to  flatten it and you want to do that for  the other side also so now you should  have something that looks just like this  okay so if you take a look at the nearly  completed rocket you can see it's kind  of flattened out so that these two legs  are next to each other and these two  legs are next to each other what you  want to do is you just want to open it  up and you want to flatten it the other  way so that these top two are next to  each other and the bottom two are next  to each other and then you want to  flatten it out and make a good crease  that way so now you should have a model  that looks like this okay so if you look  at the model you'll see what looks like  four little kites on the bottom here  what you want to do is you want to take  the corner of this kite shape and you  want to fold it in half going this way  so you want to take it and you want to  push down on it when you do that you'll  see that this edge here is kind of  dragged along with it it's holding it  back so what you want to do you want to  fold it and you want to push straight  down on that edge just like that and  flatten everything out and you want to  do that for the remaining three  alright guys we just have two folds left  and they're really easy all you have to  do is just turn the rocket over and just  open it up a little bit and just like  before when we tuck these corners in we  just want to tuck these in also so just  fold it down inside of the rocket and  then do the same for the other side and  if you hold it like this you'll see that  you have now completed your paper rocket  ship thanks a lot for watching my  tutorial for how to make the paper  rocket ship I know it was tricky so be  sure to go back and re-watch some parts  which might have given you trouble just  to make sure you're making the correct  folds if you haven't already seen my  tutorial for how to make the paper crane  the balloon and also the ninja star you  can check them out by going to my  channel videos by clicking on my name to  the right and as always be sure to  comment rate and subscribe for  notification of my future videos
 

